# Python Template

Minimal template for Python repos using `uv`, `mise`, `ruff`, `ty`, and `pytest`.

## Prerequisites

Install [mise](https://mise.jdx.dev):

```bash
brew install mise
echo 'eval "$(mise activate zsh)"' >> ~/.zshrc
source ~/.zshrc
```

## Setup

```bash
git clone <this-repo-url>
cd cloned-project
mise install
uv sync
```

## Environment Variables

This template uses `mise` to load environment-specific files from `.env/<env>/.env`.

Use `.env.example` as the starting point for each local environment:

```bash
mkdir -p .env/staging
cp .env.example .env/staging/.env
```

Examples:

```bash
mkdir -p .env/staging
cp .env.example .env/staging/.env

mkdir -p .env/production
cp .env.example .env/production/.env
```

By default, `mise` loads `.env/staging/.env`. To switch environments, set `MISE_ENV`:

```bash
MISE_ENV=production mise run test
MISE_ENV=staging mise run check
```

For a longer shell session, export it once:

```bash
export MISE_ENV=staging
mise run check
mise run test
```

Keep secrets and machine-specific values in `.env/<env>/.env`. These files are ignored by git, while `.env.example` stays committed as the shared blueprint.

## Project Layout

```text
.
├── pyproject.toml
├── README.md
├── mise.toml
├── src/
│ └── data_template/
│ └── main.py
└── tests/
    └── test_main.py
```

## Development

Run the app:

```bash
uv run python src/data_template/main.py
```

Run quality checks:

```bash
mise run lint
mise run lint-fix
mise run format
mise run format-check
mise run typecheck
mise run test
mise run check
```

Or run the tools directly:

```bash
uv run ruff check .
uv run ruff format .
uv run ty check .
uv run pytest
